# Knowledge Lifecycle States

Spec: LifecycleStates
Purpose:
  Define the state machine for knowledge lifecycle transitions
  and the rules governing each transition.

Owns: lifecycle/states.sdd

## States

### CANDIDATE
  description:
    Knowledge has been identified as potentially reusable but has not yet
    been validated by tests, tasks, or human review. Entry point for new
    knowledge entering the lifecycle.
  retention:
    30 days (candidates expire without promotion)
  actions:
    - keep in candidate index
    - exclude from standard context (P6 only)
    - flag for review by knowledge-cleaner
    - auto-expire after 30 days without evidence

### ACTIVE
  description:
    Knowledge is actively used — referenced by tasks, decisions,
    or skills in the last 7 days.
  retention:
    indefinite (while active)
  actions:
    - maintain in primary index
    - include in compiled context

### STALE
  description:
    Knowledge exists but has not been referenced for 7-30 days.
    Not yet superseded, but not actively used.
  retention:
    180 days before archive consideration
  actions:
    - keep in index with stale marker
    - exclude from standard context (P6 only)
    - flag for review by knowledge-cleaner

### DEPRECATED
  description:
    Knowledge has been superseded by newer knowledge via
    @supersedes relationship, or marked deprecated by decision.
  retention:
    90 days before archive
  actions:
    - exclude from compiled context
    - keep in deprecated index
    - generate @proposal.knowledge-archive

### SUPERSEDED
  description:
    Knowledge has been explicitly replaced by a newer entity via
    an explicit @supersedes relationship. Preserved for history;
    references should redirect to the successor.
  retention:
    90 days before archive
  actions:
    - exclude from compiled context
    - redirect references to successor
    - keep in superseded index
    - generate @proposal.knowledge-archive

### DELETE_BLOCKED
  description:
    A transient state entered when deletion is attempted on an entity
    that still has active dependencies. The entity is NOT deleted;
    deletion is blocked until all dependencies are resolved.
  retention:
    Until dependencies resolved (no auto-expiry)
  actions:
    - retain in primary index
    - block all delete operations
    - list blocking dependencies
    - notify reviewer of blocking entities

### ARCHIVED
  description:
    Knowledge is preserved for historical reference only.
    Not loaded into AI context unless explicitly requested.
  retention:
    - PUBLIC/INTERNAL: 5 years
    - CONFIDENTIAL: 10 years
    - SECRET: 15 years (encrypted)
  actions:
    - move to archive/
    - remove from primary index
    - keep reference in deprecated index

## State Transitions

  ACTIVE → STALE
    trigger: no references for 7 days
    rule: [TR-01] Automated, soft transition
    action: mark stale, notify knowledge-cleaner

  STALE → DEPRECATED
    trigger: @supersedes from another node
    OR: @decision marks deprecated
    action: record deprecation reason, set archive date

  DEPRECATED → ARCHIVED
    trigger: archive date reached OR @proposal.knowledge-archive approved
    action: move to archive/, update references

   ACTIVE → DEPRECATED
     trigger: @supersedes from another node
     action: immediate deprecation (bypasses stale)

   CANDIDATE → ACTIVE
     trigger: promotion approved (evidence + human review)
     rule: [TR-07] Promotion requires evidence_count >= 2 and human approval
     action: move to primary index, include in context

   ACTIVE → SUPERSEDED
     trigger: explicit @supersedes from a newer node
     rule: [TR-08] SUPERSEDED is triggered by explicit @supersedes, not time
     action: record successor, redirect references, keep for history

   DEPRECATED → SUPERSEDED
     trigger: explicit @supersedes from a newer node (alternative to ARCHIVED)
     action: record successor, update deprecation index

   SUPERSEDED → ARCHIVED
     trigger: archive date reached OR @proposal.knowledge-archive approved
     action: move to archive/, update references

   ANY → DELETE_BLOCKED
     trigger: delete attempted while active dependencies exist
     action: block deletion, list dependencies, notify reviewer

   DELETE_BLOCKED → target_state
     trigger: all dependencies resolved (redirected or removed)
     action: proceed with original delete/archival operation

   CANDIDATE → ARCHIVED
     trigger: candidate expired without promotion (30 days)
     action: move to archive/, preserve for history

   ARCHIVED → ACTIVE
     trigger: task explicitly requires archived knowledge
     action: restore from archive, re-evaluate quality

  ANY → ARCHIVED
    trigger: @proposal.knowledge-archive approved by human
    action: immediate archive

  ARCHIVED → ACTIVE
    trigger: task explicitly requires archived knowledge
    action: restore from archive, re-evaluate quality

## Transition Rules

  [TR-01] Active → Stale is automated after 7 days of no references.
  [TR-02] Stale → Deprecated requires human or AI evidence (@supersedes or @decision).
  [TR-03] Deprecated → Archived requires @proposal.approved.
  [TR-04] Secret/Confidential knowledge has extended retention times.
  [TR-05] Archived knowledge can be restored if explicitly referenced.
   [TR-06] AI CANNOT archive its own recent work (24-hour grace period).
   [TR-07] CANDIDATE → ACTIVE requires promotion approval per
            learning-loop.sdd promotion rules (L2 → L3).
   [TR-08] SUPERSEDED is triggered by explicit @supersedes relation,
             not by time or staleness.
   [TR-09] DELETE_BLOCKED prevents deletion until all dependencies are
           resolved (per gc-policy.sdd dependency check protocol).
   [TR-10] CANDIDATE without evidence for 7 days is auto-flagged
           for review by knowledge-cleaner.

